WEBVTT

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:34.050
<v Ira Glass>I think probably every two years, I read an article about some scientist who thinks there might be a way, building off chicken DNA or whatever, to figure out the DNA of dinosaurs and bring one to life. I feel like I run into these stories all the time. There were those scientists a couple years ago who were talking about how you could take Neanderthal DNA and use it to create new Neanderthals.
<v Ira Glass>我想大概每隔两年，我就会读到一篇关于某位科学家的文章，他认为或许有办法，比如以鸡的 DNA 为基础，弄清楚恐龙的 DNA 并让恐龙复活。我觉得我总是能碰到这类新闻。几年前就有科学家在谈论如何提取尼安德特人的 DNA，并用它来创造新的尼安德特人。

00:00:34.050 --> 00:01:01.340
<v Ira Glass>Or this is, I think, the realest one going. I think this is an actual thing. There's a team led by a Harvard scientist trying to bring back the woolly mammoth. That's right, the woolly mammoth. And have herds of them tromping through the Siberian tundra. That's the actual plan. And can I just say, I know you scientists, you have your reasons. But whenever I read this stuff, I think, did you guys not see Jurassic Park? Have we learned nothing from the movies?
<v Ira Glass>或者说，我认为这才是目前最真实的一个。我觉得这是一件真事。有一个由哈佛科学家领导的团队正试图复活猛犸象。没错，就是猛犸象。并让成群的猛犸象在西伯利亚苔原上奔跑。这就是真正的计划。我能说句公道话吗，我知道你们科学家有你们的理由。但每当我读到这些内容时，我都在想，你们难道没看过《侏罗纪公园》吗？从电影里我们什么都没学到吗？

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:05.330
<v Ian Malcolm>Your scientists were so preoccupied with whether or not they could, they didn't stop to think if they should.
<v Ian Malcolm>你们的科学家太专注于他们是否能做到，却没停下来思考他们是否应该去做。

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:22.790
<v Ira Glass>Thank you, Jeff Goldblum. Dr. Frankenstein collects the body parts of dead people, sews them together on a lab table, jolts them with some electricity-- very showy electricity, dare I say. The creature comes to life and then does things the scientist did not anticipate at all. Unintended consequences, my friends.
<v Ira Glass>谢谢你，杰夫·高布伦。弗兰肯斯坦博士收集死人的身体部位，把它们缝合在实验台上，用电流刺激它们——我敢说，那是相当华丽的电流。生物复活了，然后做了科学家们完全没预料到的事情。朋友们，这就是意想不到的后果。

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:42.740
<v Ira Glass>It's not just in the movies, by the way. Of course, as we all know, discoveries in subatomic physics left the lab. Decades later, we got nuclear bombs. Scientists constructed ways with computers to network with each other in the '60s. Now, half a century later, we end up with the Russians trolling our elections through social media.
<v Ira Glass>顺便说一句，这不仅仅发生在电影里。正如我们所知，亚原子物理学的发现走出了实验室。几十年后，我们有了核弹。科学家在 60 年代构建了计算机网络互联的方法。半个世纪后的今天，我们最终看到俄罗斯人通过社交媒体干扰我们的选举。

00:01:42.740 --> 00:02:15.090
<v Ira Glass>Cylons return to Caprica to kill all the humans who invented them. OK, that one's not real. But my point is the same. Unintended consequences-- they happen when the experiment leaves the lab. And today on our show, we have three examples, three telling examples from three very different kinds of labs, one of them-- OK, one of those labs is actually just a laboratory of human feelings, but still. From WBEZ Chicago, it's This American Life. I'm Ira Glass. Stay with us.
<v Ira Glass>赛昂人回到卡布里卡，杀死了所有发明他们的类人生物。好吧，那不是真的。但我的观点是一样的。意想不到的后果——当实验离开实验室时就会发生。今天在我们的节目中，我们有三个例子，三个来自三种截然不同的实验室的典型例子，其中一个——好吧，其中一个实验室实际上只是人类情感的实验室，但仍然算是一个实验室。来自 WBEZ 芝加哥，这是《美国生活》。我是艾拉·格拉斯。请继续收听。

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:48.400
<v Ira Glass>Act One, Breakout Star. OK, so we begin with this experiment gone wrong. Like I said, this is not a traditional experiment, not a traditional laboratory, but a laboratory of human emotion, one very familiar to lots of people. I'm talking about the reality TV show, The Bachelor. Been around for 23 seasons. Every season, of course, is romance made in a Petri dish. They throw in one guy, dozens of women. Each week, the guy ejects a few women from the Petri dish until there is just one left.
<v Ira Glass>第一幕，突围明星。好的，我们就从这个失败的实验开始。就像我说的，这不是一个传统的实验，不是一个传统的实验室，而是一个人类情感的实验室，这对很多人来说非常熟悉。我说的是真人秀节目《单身汉》。已经播出了 23 季。当然，每一季都是在培养皿中制造的浪漫。他们放进一个男人，几十个女人。每周，这个男人都会把几个女人从培养皿中剔除，直到只剩下一个。

00:02:48.400 --> 00:03:08.020
<v Ira Glass>And that's how it went until last season, when, for the first time, one of the lab subjects, a very important one, escaped the lab with, yes, unintended consequences. One of our producers, Emanuele Berry, tells what happened.
<v Ira Glass>事情一直这样持续到上一季，当时，第一次有一名实验对象，一个非常重要的对象，逃出了实验室，是的，带来了意想不到的后果。我们的制作人之一，伊曼纽尔·贝里，讲述了发生了什么。

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:29.530
<v Emanuele Berry>I've been watching The Bachelor for years, and I've never seen anything like what happened on Episode 9 of Season 23. There's this one moment that felt so real that I haven't shut up about it. OK, so, it's almost the last episode of the season. It's The Bachelor, so of course, they're filming in a romantic location, a beautiful property in Portugal.
<v Emanuele Berry>我看了《单身汉》很多年，从来没见过像第 23 季第 9 集那样的事情。有一个瞬间感觉太真实了，以至于我一直在谈论它。好吧，这几乎是这一季的最后一集了。这是《单身汉》，所以他们当然在浪漫的地方拍摄，葡萄牙的一处美丽的庄园。

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:52.070
<v Emanuele Berry>The bachelor this time around is Colton Underwood. He's 26, tall, sandy hair, handsome, a former football player. And as the show has mentioned a million times, he's a virgin. I could care less. Online, I saw fans of the show describe him as sweet and sincere. My roommate once called him America's chicken nugget.
<v Emanuele Berry>这次的单身汉是科尔顿·安德伍德。他 26 岁，个子高，沙色头发，帅气，前足球运动员。而且正如节目里提到过无数次的那样，他是处男。我一点都不在乎。在网上，我看到节目的粉丝形容他温柔真诚。我的室友曾叫他“美国的炸鸡块”。

00:03:52.070 --> 00:03:56.490
<v Colton Underwood>I'm here to fall in love, so hopefully, by the end of this, I am down on one knee.
<v Colton Underwood>我来这里是为了坠入爱河，所以希望在结束时，我能单膝下跪。

00:03:56.490 --> 00:04:24.100
<v Emanuele Berry>This show is a Monday night tradition in my apartment. My roommate and I open a bottle of red wine, and for two hours, we enjoy some choreographed drama, contestants who aren't there for the right reason, bachelors who didn't know it would be so hard, tearful eliminations. The entire thing, it's kind of silly. It's actually a total mess, but I'm so into it.
<v Emanuele Berry>这个节目是我公寓里周一晚上的传统。我和室友会开一瓶红酒，花两个小时欣赏精心编排的戏剧，不怀好意参赛的选手，觉得这事儿太难的单身汉，还有泪流满面的淘汰过程。整件事，有点傻。其实完全是一团糟，但我却深陷其中。

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:34.090
<v Emanuele Berry>So back to that dramatic moment. It's nighttime in Portugal, and Colton has been dumped by the girl of his dreams. He has shut himself into his room.
<v Emanuele Berry>回到那个戏剧性的时刻。那是葡萄牙的夜晚，科尔顿被他梦寐以求的女孩甩了。他把自己关在房间里。

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:39.410
<v Colton Underwood>[BLEEP] I'm done. I'm done with this.
<v Colton Underwood>[哔] 我受够了。我受够了。

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:49.960
<v Emanuele Berry>He says, "I'm done. I'm done with this." Cue the most dramatic music. He throws open the door, and his hand is suddenly covering the entire TV screen.
<v Emanuele Berry>他说：“我受够了。我受够了。”配上最戏剧性的音乐。他猛地打开门，他的手突然挡住了整个电视屏幕。

00:04:49.960 --> 00:05:05.640
<v Emanuele Berry>Then this strange thing happens. Suddenly, the invisible TV crew becomes very visible. Cameramen find their way into the frame. Colton is running down the stairs. He's taking off his mic, and the producers start calling for Chris.
<v Emanuele Berry>然后发生了奇怪的事情。突然，隐形的电视摄制组变得非常显眼。摄影师进入了画面。科尔顿跑下楼梯。他正在摘下麦克风，制片人开始呼叫克里斯。

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:08.540
<v Producer>Somebody get Chris.
<v Producer>找个人去叫克里斯。

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:42.050
<v Emanuele Berry>Chris Harrison is the host of the show, who's forever popping into scenes unannounced. And I always feel like, wait, why are you here? Colton's walking away from Chris, ignoring everyone. And then he reaches this big white fence, like an industrial security gate. It's maybe like eight feet tall. And without hesitation, in one powerful, graceful movement, he leaps up and pulls himself over. He's on the other side in a heartbeat. It's the type of move Captain America would do.
<v Emanuele Berry>克里斯·哈里森是节目的主持人，总是会不请自来地闯入场景。我总是觉得，等等，你为什么在这里？科尔顿走开，无视所有人。然后他到达了一道白色大围栏，像是一道工业安全门。大概有八英尺高。他没有犹豫，用一个有力、优雅的动作，跳了起来，把自己拉了过去。转眼间他就在围栏对面了。那是美国队长才会做的动作。

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:47.600
<v Emanuele Berry>And then Chris Harrison utters what is perhaps my favorite line in the history of The Bachelor.
<v Emanuele Berry>然后克里斯·哈里森说出了我最喜欢的台词，或许是《单身汉》历史上最棒的。

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:53.100
<v Chris Harrison>He just jumped the [BLEEP] fence. Is there a button that opens the gate?
<v Chris Harrison>他刚才竟然跳过了那道[哔]围栏。有没有能打开门的按钮？

00:05:53.100 --> 00:06:00.750
<v Emanuele Berry>The crew takes what feels like a while to actually get the gate open. And when they finally do, Colton is gone.
<v Emanuele Berry>工作人员花了很长时间才真正打开门。当他们终于打开时，科尔顿已经不见了。

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:02.930
<v Chris Harrison>He is gone.
<v Chris Harrison>他消失了。

00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:14.370
<v Emanuele Berry>The bachelor has escaped. For three minutes, I watch as they search for him, calling his name. Someone starts whistling like they're looking for a dog.
<v Emanuele Berry>单身汉逃走了。三分钟里，我看着他们到处找他，呼唤他的名字。有人开始吹口哨，好像在找狗。

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:16.110
<v Emanuele Berry>[WHISTLING]
<v Emanuele Berry>[口哨声]

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:17.250
<v Chris Harrison>Colton!
<v Chris Harrison>科尔顿！

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:18.550
<v Woman>Colton!
<v Woman>科尔顿！

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:19.740
<v Chris Harrison>I have no idea where he went.
<v Chris Harrison>我不知道他去哪儿了。

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:20.450
<v Man>Colton.
<v Man>科尔顿。

00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:26.990
<v Emanuele Berry>They get into cars, and they're driving around. And finally, they spot him on the side of the road.
<v Emanuele Berry>他们上了车，在周围开车寻找。最后，他们在路边发现了他的身影。

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:29.560
<v Woman>I'm asking if you're OK.
<v Woman>我在问你还好吗。

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:32.040
<v Colton Underwood>No, I'm not OK.
<v Colton Underwood>不，我不好。

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:54.060
<v Emanuele Berry>Colton keeps walking away. Chris tries to get him to talk. Manages to get him to walk toward a car, but Colton insists it's over. He says, I can't do this. I'm done. Then commercial. And when we come back, it's the next day, and it's bright and sunny. And Chris Harrison is knocking on Colton's door to talk.
<v Emanuele Berry>科尔顿继续走开。克里斯试图让他谈谈。设法让他走向一辆车，但科尔顿坚持说一切都结束了。他说，我做不到。我受够了。然后是广告。当我们回来时，已经是第二天了，阳光明媚。克里斯·哈里森正在敲科尔顿的房门想谈谈。

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:55.370
<v Emanuele Berry>[KNOCKING]
<v Emanuele Berry>[敲门声]

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:58.270
<v Emanuele Berry>And it all feels sort of normal.
<v Emanuele Berry>一切看起来都很正常。

00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:05.070
<v Chris Harrison>Hey, brother. What's up? Yo, man.
<v Chris Harrison>嘿，兄弟。怎么了？哟，伙计。

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:21.030
<v Emanuele Berry>And I'm watching at home, and I'm confused. Like, didn't he just say he was done with the show? Yet here he is, talking with Chris, planning his next move. On the show, it's never explained how Colton went from running away and quitting to being back in front of the cameras.
<v Emanuele Berry>我在家里看的时候，我很困惑。他刚才不是说他不录节目了吗？可他现在却在这里，和克里斯谈话，计划下一步行动。节目里从没解释过科尔顿是如何从逃跑退出变成重新回到镜头前的。

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:34.590
<v Emanuele Berry>Like, where did he go? How long was he gone? And most important, what made him decide to come back? Like, what actually happened? The TV show gave no satisfying answer to any of that. So--
<v Emanuele Berry>比如，他去哪儿了？他离开了多久？最重要的是，是什么让他决定回来的？实际上到底发生了什么？电视节目对这些问题没有给出令人满意的答案。所以——

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:36.250
<v Emanuele Berry>Hey, Colton.
<v Emanuele Berry>嘿，科尔顿。

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:37.240
<v Colton Underwood>Hey, how are you?
<v Colton Underwood>嘿，你好吗？

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:38.430
<v Emanuele Berry>Good, how are you doing?
<v Emanuele Berry>很好，你呢？

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:47.220
<v Ira Glass>I called him. Colton says when he signed up to be the bachelor, he'd already been on The Bachelorette, so he believed he understood how the show worked.
<v Ira Glass>我给他打了电话。科尔顿说当他签约成为单身汉时，他已经参加过《单身女郎》，所以他以为他了解这个节目的运作方式。

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:51.750
<v Colton Underwood>I thought that I did. I thought that I had a lot of it figured out, and I was wrong.
<v Colton Underwood>我以为我了解。我以为我把很多事情都想通了，但我错了。

00:07:51.750 --> 00:08:13.500
<v Emanuele Berry>He explained that the whole fence jump goes back to a confusion of his own making. So on each episode, there are dates with the bachelor. Some are one-on-one. Some are big group dates. And sometimes contestants don't get selected for a date at all, which sucks, because it's really the only time you get to spend with the bachelor.
<v Emanuele Berry>他解释说，跳围栏的整件事源于他自己造成的困惑。在每一集中，都有和单身汉的约会。有些是单独约会。有些是大型集体约会。有时选手根本没被选中去约会，这很糟糕，因为这确实是你唯一能和单身汉相处的时间。

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:26.430
<v Emanuele Berry>And Colton told me something I didn't know watching the show, that to figure out who goes on these dates, producers are constantly checking in with the bachelor to figure out who he likes. Like, one of the women he initially hit it off with was Hannah.
<v Emanuele Berry>科尔顿告诉我一些我在看节目时不知道的事，为了确定谁去约会，制片人会不断地询问单身汉谁是他喜欢的。比如，他最初合得来的女性之一是汉娜。

00:08:26.430 --> 00:08:34.720
<v Colton Underwood>They always asked to rank the girls. And very early on, Hannah was up there. And she got left off of a date.
<v Colton Underwood>他们总是要求给女孩们排名。很早的时候，汉娜就在榜单前列。但她却没被安排约会。

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:42.510
<v Emanuele Berry>In other words, in the beginning when there were over 20 contestants, this woman Hannah was his number one pick. But they didn't schedule a date with her.
<v Emanuele Berry>换句话说，在刚开始有 20 多名选手的时候，这个叫汉娜的女人是他的首选。但他们没安排她去约会。

00:08:42.510 --> 00:09:07.380
<v Colton Underwood>And I sort of recall remember feeling a little burnt when they did that. I was like, so let me get this straight. Hannah's number one on my list right now, and she's not getting a date this week. So from there on out, I was like, all right, if you're going to do that to my top girls, I'm not really going to tell you who my top girls are. Because I don't want you messing with them. So in a weird way, I tried to defend myself and defend the girls by not being truthful to them who my top was.
<v Colton Underwood>我记得当时感觉有点受伤。我就想，好吧，让我理清一下。汉娜在我的名单上排名第一，可她这周却没有约会。所以从那时起，我就想，好吧，如果你们要那样对待我最喜欢的女孩，我就不会再告诉你们谁是我真正的首选了。因为我不想让你们干扰她们。所以以一种奇怪的方式，我试图保护自己，保护那些女孩，通过不告诉他们谁是我真正的首选。

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:10.420
<v Emanuele Berry>So even after Hannah stopped being his favorite.
<v Emanuele Berry>所以即便在汉娜不再是他的最爱之后。

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:17.070
<v Colton Underwood>I just kept the top the same. So Hannah was always at the top of the list when I always made the list for them to see, and I never changed it.
<v Colton Underwood>我还是保持名单不变。所以当每次我给他们看名单时，汉娜总是在最前面，我从未改过。

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:31.080
<v Emanuele Berry>It's so interesting because it feels like you're learning their game and then coming up with ways to sort of like either foil it, or protect yourself, or put yourself in a better position. Like, did you find yourself doing that throughout the entire process?
<v Emanuele Berry>这太有趣了，因为感觉你是在学习他们的套路，然后想出一些方法来挫败他们，或者保护自己，或者让自己处于更有利的位置。你在整个过程中都发现自己在这样做吗？

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:35.520
<v Colton Underwood>Well, yeah. So like, that's just me wanting to set myself up for success.
<v Colton Underwood>嗯，是的。这就是我想为自己成功创造条件。

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:43.390
<v Emanuele Berry>While Colton kept putting Hannah as his number one pick each week, the girl he fell for hardest was actually Cassie.
<v Emanuele Berry>虽然科尔顿每周都把汉娜放在第一位，但他最动心的女孩其实是凯西。

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:43.880
<v Cassie>How are you?
<v Cassie>你好吗？

00:09:43.880 --> 00:09:45.600
<v Colton Underwood>You look amazing. How are you?
<v Colton Underwood>你看上去美极了。你好吗？

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:55.680
<v Cassie>Good. On a scale of one to hot, Colton is hot. I feel like we do have some chemistry, and I'm looking forward to just diving right in.
<v Cassie>很好。按性感程度从一到十来算，科尔顿很性感。我觉得我们确实有火花，我期待着直接投入其中。

00:09:55.680 --> 00:10:06.030
<v Emanuele Berry>She's got a surfer vibe, blonde hair, beachy waves. They had chemistry. But as a viewer, she didn't seem like a frontrunner. I kind of kept forgetting who Cassie was.
<v Emanuele Berry>她有一种冲浪者的气质，金发，海滩波浪卷。他们有火花。但作为观众，她看起来并不像领跑者。我总是不停地忘记凯西是谁。

00:10:06.030 --> 00:10:37.990
<v Colton Underwood>I think with Cass, the best way to describe our relationship is it was such a slow burn. And it was, in a weird way, in the dynamic of The Bachelor franchise where it's supposed to be quick, and fast, and intense, it was sort of a relief to find a normal relationship in which it was a slower burn, and which it was a more realistic approach to a relationship. And I think it was just, it was almost like when I was with Cass, it was like a breath of fresh air.
<v Colton Underwood>我认为对于凯西，形容我们关系的最好方式是，这是一种慢热。用一种奇怪的方式，在《单身汉》这个本应快速、激烈、紧凑的系列节目中，能找到一段正常的、慢热的关系，以一种更现实的方式对待一段关系，这算是一种解脱。我觉得那就像，我和凯西在一起时，就像呼吸到了一口新鲜空气。

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:57.120
<v Emanuele Berry>So toward the end of the season, they're down to just three women-- Cassie, his favorite, Hannah, who the producers think is his favorite, and Tayshia, the token black girl. They're all in Portugal, and they each have an overnight date scheduled with Colton. But someone has to be eliminated by the end of the episode.
<v Emanuele Berry>所以到了这一季接近尾声时，只剩下三位女性——凯西，他最喜欢的；汉娜，制片人以为是他最喜欢的；还有泰莎，那个黑人代表。她们都在葡萄牙，每人都安排了和科尔顿的过夜约会。但这一集结束时必须淘汰一个人。

00:10:57.120 --> 00:11:23.100
<v Emanuele Berry>I don't know exactly what the producers intended. They declined my request for an interview. But watching the show, it seemed like they were trying to get Cassie to quit. They threw a wrench in her and Colton's relationship, a wrench shaped like Cassie's dad. Colton had met Cassie's dad in an earlier episode when he asked for permission to propose. Mind you, he did this for nearly all the remaining contestants. But Cassie's dad said no.
<v Emanuele Berry>我不知道制片人具体想要什么。他们拒绝了我的采访请求。但看节目时，看起来他们是想让凯西退出。他们给凯西和科尔顿的关系制造了障碍，这个障碍的形状就是凯西的爸爸。科尔顿在早些时候的一集里见过凯西的爸爸，当时他请求准许求婚。请注意，他对几乎所有剩下的选手都这么做了。但凯西的爸爸说不。

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:30.490
<v Dad>So I feel like as far as the hand of marriage, that would be a premature blessing.
<v Dad>我觉得谈到婚姻，这是一个过早的祝福。

00:11:30.490 --> 00:11:37.230
<v Colton Underwood>I see where you're coming from. That's not exactly what I wanted to hear.
<v Colton Underwood>我明白你的意思了。这并不是我真正想听到的。

00:11:37.230 --> 00:11:53.220
<v Emanuele Berry>A week later in Portugal, Colton's certain about Cassie. Cassie's confused. Again, I have no idea what the producers were thinking. But when I was watching it, it seemed like they were forcing Cassie's hand. The show allows a special guest to visit.
<v Emanuele Berry>一周后在葡萄牙，科尔顿确定了凯西。凯西感到困惑。再说一次，我不知道制片人在想什么。但当我观看时，看起来他们是在强迫凯西。节目允许特殊嘉宾访问。

00:11:53.220 --> 00:12:08.980
<v Colton Underwood>Later, in that episode, her dad actually shows up, which nobody just accidentally shows up in Portugal. So the producers paid a pretty hefty price to fly that man on out to Portugal to come visit and spend time with his daughter to give her clarity.
<v Colton Underwood>在那一集后期，她的父亲真的出现了，没人会无缘无故出现在葡萄牙。所以制片人付出了高昂的代价把那个人飞到葡萄牙，来探望并花时间与他的女儿相处，好让她清醒。

00:12:08.980 --> 00:12:12.850
<v Emanuele Berry>Cassie's dad talks to her, and she decides to leave the show.
<v Emanuele Berry>凯西的爸爸和她谈过之后，她决定离开节目。

00:12:12.850 --> 00:12:25.090
<v Dad>There shouldn't be any hesitation in your mind when you meet somebody that you want to spend the rest of your life with. None. It's a lifelong decision. It's not something you make if you're unsure.
<v Dad>当你遇到一个想要共度余生的人时，你的内心不应该有任何犹豫。一点都没有。这是一个终身的决定。如果你不确定，就不应该做这个决定。

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:27.400
<v Emanuele Berry>Cassie decides to tell Colton at dinner.
<v Emanuele Berry>凯西决定在晚餐时告诉科尔顿。

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:52.460
<v Colton Underwood>Normally, during the dinners and during that, the producers are sort of hovering, or they're around to help the conversation flow. Or they're there just to, like, bounce ideas off of when you guys are talking. When we had that dinner, there wasn't a producer in sight. There was just the cameras, and there was just the audios. Everybody else ran. And they didn't want to be near it because I think they knew that I knew.
<v Colton Underwood>通常，在晚餐期间，制片人会游荡在附近，帮助对话顺利进行。或者他们就在旁边，好让你们谈话时能蹦出些点子。当我们吃那顿晚餐时，周围一个制片人都看不见。只有摄像机，只有音频设备。其他人都跑了。他们不想靠近那里，因为我想他们知道我也知道内情。

00:12:52.460 --> 00:13:10.110
<v Emanuele Berry>Knew that they set him up, he means. At dinner, Cassie tells him she's leaving. And she mentions that her dad is here in Portugal and that they've been talking. Colton clearly has no idea that this was happening. And he turns as though looking for someone.
<v Emanuele Berry>知道他们设套陷害他，他是这个意思。在晚餐时，凯西告诉他她要离开了。她提到她爸爸就在葡萄牙，他们一直在谈话。科尔顿显然不知道这一切正在发生。他转身，仿佛在寻找某个人。

00:13:10.110 --> 00:13:27.160
<v Colton Underwood>Oh, I was thinking I just got screwed. I was thinking that that wasn't her doing. I know what the format of the show is. And for me hearing, hey, by the way, my dad came back, really sparked something in me. I was like, OK. So I don't have the control I thought I had.
<v Colton Underwood>噢，我当时想我被坑惨了。我当时想那不是她自愿做的。我知道节目的套路是什么。听到那句，嘿，顺便说一下，我爸爸来了，真的触发了我的某种情绪。我就想，好吧。所以我并没有我想象中那么有掌控力。

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:43.630
<v Colton Underwood>If I feel like my relationship's going to be messed with or toyed with at all, I'm going to be done. Especially at this point, I've completely fallen in love. I've completely, like, gave myself all to her. I mean, I had nothing to lose at that point besides the girl and the woman that I wanted to spend the rest of my life with.
<v Colton Underwood>如果我感觉到我的关系会被搞乱或被摆布，我就会退出。特别是在这个阶段，我已经完全坠入爱河。我已经完全，把自己的一切都给了她。我的意思是，除了那个我想共度余生的女孩，我已经没什么可失去的了。

00:13:43.630 --> 00:14:04.550
<v Emanuele Berry>So Colton's about to lose the girl that he loves. And in a perverse way, it's kind of his fault. When Colton started lying about who he liked most on his list, the show's not really built for that. It's as if an inanimate test subject suddenly became sentient. Basically, he compromised the entire experiment. He sort of played himself.
<v Emanuele Berry>所以科尔顿快要失去他深爱的女孩了。而且以一种荒谬的方式，这某种程度上是他的错。当科尔顿开始撒谎说谁是他名单上最喜欢的女孩时，节目本身并没有针对这种情况构建规则。这就好像一个无生命的测试对象突然有了知觉。基本上，他破坏了整个实验。他把自己玩砸了。

00:14:04.550 --> 00:14:13.090
<v Colton Underwood>I think that it backfired because then they were like, whoa, we thought it was Hannah because you kept telling us even on your list, when you'd rank them, Hannah's one.
<v Colton Underwood>我觉得这适得其反，因为他们当时想，哇，我们以为是汉娜，因为你一直告诉我们，即使在你的名单上，当你给她们排名时，汉娜也是第一。

00:14:13.090 --> 00:14:20.020
<v Emanuele Berry>And so in the end, Cassie ends up basically sort of breaking up with you and leaving, right?
<v Emanuele Berry>所以最后，凯西基本上和你分手并离开了，对吧？

00:14:20.020 --> 00:14:40.390
<v Colton Underwood>Yeah. So we walk, and I just get up and we start walking to the car. And it was in the dark. I remember there was a sidewalk we were supposed to stay on. It was completely lit, and I was like, we're not staying on the sidewalk. Like, I started-- right then and there, I was like, I'm not doing showy things anymore. I'm not doing things just to go through the motions of being the bachelor.
<v Colton Underwood>是的。所以我们走着，我站起身，开始走向那辆车。当时天很黑。我记得有一条我们本应该待在上面的人行道。灯火通明，而我说，我们不待在人行道上了。当时就在那一刻，我心想，我不再做那些表演性质的事了。我不再仅仅为了完成作为“单身汉”的例行公事而做那些事了。

00:14:40.390 --> 00:15:04.060
<v Colton Underwood>So I was starting to run through scenarios in my head as I put her in the van and said goodbye to her. I was like, all right, I'm going to go upstairs. I'm going to grab my wallet. First off, I got to get away from these people. I have to lose my mic. I have to lose the cameras. I have to just be by myself. And my plan was to get out of there and go grab a new passport, because they did have my passport. So I was like, I got my wallet. I have--
<v Colton Underwood>所以我当时脑子里开始闪过各种场景，当我把她放进面包车并和她告别时。我就想，好吧，我要上楼。我要拿我的钱包。首先，我必须离开这些人。我必须摆脱我的麦克风。我必须摆脱摄像机。我必须一个人待着。我的计划是离开那里，去拿一本新护照，因为他们拿走了我的护照。所以我当时想，我拿到了钱包。我有——

00:15:04.060 --> 00:15:06.220
<v Emanuele Berry>Wait. You're like, I'm going to go get a new passport?
<v Emanuele Berry>等等。你是说，你要去弄一本新护照？

00:15:06.220 --> 00:15:20.570
<v Colton Underwood>I'm done. I wanted to be done. I didn't want to talk to the people on the show. I was about to pay for my own flight to get home. I literally was done talking to everybody. So I went up, I grabbed my wallet, and I remember opening the door and the first thing I see is a camera right there.
<v Colton Underwood>我受够了。我想彻底结束。我不想和节目组的人谈话。我当时准备自己掏钱买机票回家。我真的不想再和任何人谈话了。所以我上楼，拿了钱包，我记得我打开门，第一眼看到的就是一个摄像机就在那儿。

00:15:20.570 --> 00:15:38.710
<v Colton Underwood>And if I had any regrets from the night, the only regret would be is actually hitting and putting a hand on the camera because that's not my property. But I was heated, so I hit the camera just to get it out of my way and went down the stairs. And that's when I undid my mic.
<v Colton Underwood>如果说那天晚上有什么后悔的事，唯一的遗憾就是打了那台摄像机，因为那不是我的财产。但我当时太火大了，我就打了摄像机把它移开，然后跑下楼梯。就在那时我摘下了麦克风。

00:15:38.710 --> 00:15:56.000
<v Colton Underwood>And once I did that, I think they had an idea of what was coming next. And I remember walking up to the fence, and I had no clue how to open it. I didn't want to wait for people to open it. So without hesitation, without even thinking, I was just like, screw it. I'm over this thing. Let's do it.
<v Colton Underwood>当我做完那件事，我想他们大概预料到接下来会发生什么了。我记得走向围栏，我根本不知道怎么打开它。我不想等着别人来开。所以没有犹豫，甚至没多想，我就想，去他的。我不玩了。干吧。

00:15:56.000 --> 00:16:24.270
<v Colton Underwood>And I just gathered myself and jumped over the fence, fully expecting the other side to have people, producers, handlers, the food tent. I mean, the scale of this show is so big that there's people everywhere. You can never get by yourself. I mean, there are so many hands on deck, all of these things. But I jumped the fence, and there was nothing. It was darkness. It was fields.
<v Colton Underwood>我就调整了一下重心，跳过了围栏，完全以为围栏另一边会有工作人员、制片人、随行人员、餐饮帐篷。我的意思是，这个节目的规模太大了，到处都是人。你永远没法独自待着。我的意思是，有那么多人手在忙，所有这些东西。但我跳过围栏后，什么都没有。只有黑暗。只有田野。

00:16:24.270 --> 00:16:32.200
<v Colton Underwood>And for me, I was like, this is awesome. So I was like, I'm here. I was like, I don't want them to catch up. So I started running.
<v Colton Underwood>对我来说，我就想，这太棒了。所以我就想，我到了。我就想，我不想让他们追上。所以我开始跑。

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:34.210
<v Emanuele Berry>So you ran, and you took off.
<v Emanuele Berry>所以你跑了，你逃走了。

00:16:34.210 --> 00:16:50.410
<v Colton Underwood>I ran, and I took off. And I'm the worst with directions. Like, I'm very directionally challenged. And I had no clue where I was going. I remember having a ton of bright lights over to the left, so I was like, I'm just going to run towards the lights. And hopefully, I get there.
<v Colton Underwood>我跑了，我逃走了。而且我是个方向感极差的人。我的意思是，我的方向感非常糟糕。我完全不知道我要去哪儿。我记得左边有一大堆明亮的灯光，所以我当时想，我就往灯光那边跑吧。希望我能到那里。

00:16:50.410 --> 00:17:08.410
<v Colton Underwood>Granted, these lights are, like, 40 miles away, 30 miles away. I was like, let's do it. I was running in boots and tight jeans, which is the worst combination ever to run in. And I remember hearing in the distance the producers start yelling my name, so I knew they were chasing after me.
<v Colton Underwood>当然，这些灯光离我有 40 英里远，30 英里远。我心想，就这么干吧。我穿着靴子和紧身牛仔裤在跑，这是跑步时最糟糕的搭配了。我记得在远处听到制片人开始大声喊我的名字，所以我知道他们在追我。

00:17:08.410 --> 00:17:13.510
<v Emanuele Berry>Where did you hide? You're a big dude. Were you hiding behind a tree? Were you in bushes?
<v Emanuele Berry>你躲哪儿去了？你是个大块头。你躲在树后面了吗？你在灌木丛里吗？

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:26.210
<v Colton Underwood>Oh. It was dangerous, too, because I had no clue what the laws were in Portugal. I was hopping personal fences. I was hiding behind people's cars. I was laying down in ditches.
<v Colton Underwood>噢。那也很危险，因为我根本不知道葡萄牙的法律是什么。我翻过私人的围栏。我躲在别人的车后面。我躺在沟里。

00:17:26.210 --> 00:17:51.650
<v Colton Underwood>And finally, I hopped through a backyard, and there was like a chain link fence. And all of a sudden, I hear these animals. And they sort of sounded like dogs, and I love dogs. I'm a big dog person. But this was like an aggressive, growling, howling thing. And I was like, all right, this is probably a little dangerous. I probably am a little in over my head here, trying to get back and find a passport. So I'll just turn myself in. I was gone for about a good two hours.
<v Colton Underwood>最后，我翻进了一个后院，那里有一个铁丝网围栏。突然，我听到了一些动物的声音。听起来像是狗，我爱狗。我是一个超级爱狗的人。但那听起来像是一种好斗的、咆哮的、嚎叫的东西。我就想，好吧，这大概有点危险。我可能是有点自不量力了，试图逃走并找护照。所以我还是自首吧。我消失了大概有两个小时。

00:17:51.650 --> 00:17:54.150
<v Emanuele Berry>You were gone for two hours?
<v Emanuele Berry>你消失了两个小时？

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:57.530
<v Colton Underwood>It was yeah, when it's all said and done.
<v Colton Underwood>是的，当一切结束的时候。

00:17:57.530 --> 00:18:12.170
<v Emanuele Berry>So he turns himself in. Not to police, of course, but to reality TV. He does this by walking to the main road till someone finds him. When they do, he's still upset, and overwhelmed, and not ready to talk.
<v Emanuele Berry>所以他自首了。当然不是向警察，而是向真人秀节目。他走到大路上直到有人发现他。当他们找到他时，他仍然很难过，精疲力竭，还没准备好谈话。

00:18:12.170 --> 00:18:29.540
<v Emanuele Berry>So he plays the system. He says there's a rule that you cannot be filmed or recorded while talking to the show's therapist. So he asked for that. He says they talked for an hour while he vented and figured out his next move. And then finally, he was ready to talk to producers.
<v Emanuele Berry>于是他玩了套路。他说有一条规定，在和节目心理医生谈话时不能被拍摄或记录。所以他要求这样做。他说他们谈了一个小时，他发泄了情绪并想出了下一步打算。最后，他才准备好和制片人谈话。

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:41.120
<v Emanuele Berry>What was that game plan or that conversation like? Did they have to convince you to come back? Because at that point, you were saying that you were done, right? If Cassie wasn't going to be there, you were like-- you seemed very done also.
<v Emanuele Berry>那个计划或者谈话是什么样的？他们必须说服你回来吗？因为在那一刻，你说过你不想玩了，对吧？如果凯西不在那里，你当时显得——看起来你也非常坚定地想离开。

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:42.350
<v Colton Underwood>Yeah. Yes, so the game plan--
<v Colton Underwood>是的。是的，所以计划是——

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:48.180
<v Emanuele Berry>Yeah, what was the conversation like to get you to come back to the show?
<v Emanuele Berry>是的，说服你回到节目的谈话是什么样的？

00:18:48.180 --> 00:18:58.940
<v Colton Underwood>So the conversation was-- well, obviously, they just wanted to hear me out. They wanted to hear what I had to say. And then the game plan was to talk to Cass again, but I only wanted to do that after I talked to the other two women.
<v Colton Underwood>所以谈话内容是——嗯，很明显，他们只是想听听我的想法。他们想听听我要说什么。然后计划是再次和凯西谈谈，但我只想在我和另外两个女人谈话之后才这么做。

00:18:58.940 --> 00:19:26.630
<v Emanuele Berry>The lab rat is suddenly running the lab. Colton wants to break up with the other two contestants, so he can make it clear to Cassie that she's the one that he wants and they don't have to get married. This goes totally against the show's format. It means no final two, no big bro ceremony, no proposal scene. All of these sacred touchstones are just gone from the show. It's like watching the Olympics without the medal ceremony at the end.
<v Emanuele Berry>实验鼠突然开始操控实验室了。科尔顿想和另外两个参赛者分手，这样他就能明确告诉凯西她是他的心仪对象，而且他们不必结婚。这完全违背了节目的格式。这意味着没有终极两人组，没有盛大的求婚仪式，没有求婚场景。所有这些神圣的里程碑都从节目中消失了。这就像在看没有颁奖仪式的奥运会一样。

00:19:26.630 --> 00:19:33.840
<v Emanuele Berry>So you felt like you sort of had more power or maybe a little more leverage to have control when you went back.
<v Emanuele Berry>所以你觉得当你回去时，你拥有了更多的权力或更多筹码来掌握控制权。

00:19:33.840 --> 00:19:53.280
<v Colton Underwood>Well, I think it was just me-- they knew I was serious. Like, it's one thing when leads say, OK, I'm done. Like, it's OK, but you turn around, and you're in an interview the next minute. It's like, you're not done. You're sitting right in front of them. You're doing exactly what they want you to do. So they knew not to really cross that line.
<v Colton Underwood>嗯，我觉得这只是我——他们知道我是认真的。我的意思是，当领头的人说“好吧，我受够了”，这是一回事。虽然看起来还行，但你转过身，下一分钟你就坐在访谈室里了。这就说明你没受够。你就坐在他们面前。你在做他们想要你做的一切。所以他们知道不要真的越过那条线。

00:19:53.280 --> 00:20:09.990
<v Emanuele Berry>In the end, he gets what he wants. He talks to Cassie. They decide to date and not get engaged. Colton is still friends with the producers. And he says he and Cassie are still together and very happy.
<v Emanuele Berry>最后，他得到了他想要的。他和凯西谈了。他们决定约会而不订婚。科尔顿和制片人还是朋友。他说他和凯西现在依然在一起，非常幸福。

